# Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
# Set @host to the URL printed by `dotnet run` (see Properties/launchSettings.json).
@host = http://localhost:5103

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### Register a user
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "Passw0rd!123" }

### Login (named request, token reused below)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "Passw0rd!123" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Balance
GET {{host}}/wallet
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deposit 500.00 ETB (50000 minor units). Send it twice: the second reply has Idempotent-Replayed: true
POST {{host}}/wallet/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: dep-0002
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 50000 }

### Same key, different amount => 422 idempotency_key_reuse
POST {{host}}/wallet/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: dep-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 99999 }

### Withdraw 100.00 ETB
POST {{host}}/wallet/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: wd-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 10000 }

### Withdraw more than the balance => 422 insufficient_funds
POST {{host}}/wallet/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: wd-0002
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 99999999 }

### Missing Idempotency-Key => 400
POST {{host}}/wallet/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 100 }

### Transaction history
GET {{host}}/wallet/transactions?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### No token => 401
GET {{host}}/wallet
